# Product & Cost Guardrails

Canonical docs (read when changing product/backend direction):

- `docs/PRODUCT.md` — product vision
- `docs/TECH.md` — stack, cost, folder conventions
- `docs/USER_JOURNEY.md` — backend journey steps

## Cost

Stay **$0** until real users or Spark Pass revenue: no Stripe/Sentry/paid moderation. Redis is part of the stack — free tier or self-hosted, never a paid Redis plan. Hosting target: Oracle Always Free (2 OCPU / 12 GB), ~$5/mo VPS as the fallback.

Approved at $0 (self-hosted or free tier, no vendor contract):

- **Redis** — free tier (Upstash/Redis Cloud) for dev, and **self-hosted on the same VM** once off the laptop; anonymous matchmaking only (rooms are in-process).
- **JokeAPI v2** (no key, no cost) for meme text and the public **Memegen.link** instance (`api.memegen.link`) for rendering. Not KLIPY — KLIPY stays the chat GIF provider only. The browser contacts Memegen directly (disclosed in Privacy).
- **A production domain** — one-off purchase, approved when UGC memes (R2 custom domain) or leaving Render forces it (D11: deferred until then).
- **FCM web push** — Firebase Cloud Messaging is free with no quota charge. Optional and
  OFF by default (all `FCM_*` env vars must be set). Transport only: no Firebase Auth/DB/Analytics.
  Pushes never carry message text.
- **Cloudflare Turnstile** — free, no quota charge. Optional: set both `TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` and
  `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY`, else the weak arithmetic fallback runs (dev/CI). Third-party script that loads
  only on a guest's first room post (disclosed in Privacy + Cookies).
- **Analytics** — a self-hosted/free collector via `VITE_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT`
  (see `client/src/shared/lib/analytics.ts`). Disabled when the var is unset.
  Never a paid product (no Sentry/PostHog/Amplitude paid tier) without a new
  entry here.

## Stack baseline

**Server:** Node 22+, Express 5, Mongoose 9, Socket.IO 4.8+, Zod 4, TypeScript 7.

**Client:** React 19, Vite 8, React Router 7, Tailwind 4, TanStack Query 5, Zustand 5, Zod 4, TypeScript 7. Phase 2 must follow the same majors — no parallel older stack.

## Auth note

Connected layer currently uses a single access JWT cookie. Prefer access+refresh when hardening auth. Do not add unused `REFRESH_TOKEN_*` env keys. Admin uses a separate httpOnly `adminToken` cookie (never put `ADMIN_SECRET` in `VITE_*`).
